  "fieldDeltas": [
    {
      "requirementId": "FR-CPU-004",
      "kind": "fr",
      "acId": "ac-03",
      "beforeText": "Bit 3 controls the cassette motor (active low).",
      "afterText": "On C64, the cassette motor output is active low from DDR-masked bit 5, !(DDR & DATA & 0x20), and the cassette write output is bit 3, (~DDR | DATA) & 0x08. Match pinned VICE's changed-effective-output detection for data and DDR writes, including input/output transitions and repeated writes. Do not exchange the motor and write bits.",
      "alsoReplaceExactBodySentence": true,
      "expectedBodyOccurrences": 1,
      "bodyBeforeSha256": "AD7DA25894049B50A4066A6DF82499D19E2A8A00D83BEC988DD5F57584A0ABBC",
      "statusBefore": "pending",
      "isSatisfiedBefore": false,
      "statusAfter": "pending",
      "isSatisfiedAfter": false
    },
    {
      "requirementId": "FR-CPU-004",
      "kind": "fr",
      "acId": "ac-05",
      "beforeText": "Bit 5 is unused on C64 but reads as expected based on DDR/pull-up behavior.",
      "afterText": "On the C64 board, reading $0001 with DDR bit 5 clear returns bit 5 clear; with DDR bit 5 set, its output readback follows pinned VICE's port data/DDR calculation. Bit 5 is the motor-control bit, not an unused pin. Exercise both data levels, both DDR directions, and direction changes; do not substitute SX-64 floating-pin behavior for C64 behavior.",
      "alsoReplaceExactBodySentence": true,
      "expectedBodyOccurrences": 1,
      "bodyBeforeSha256": "AD7DA25894049B50A4066A6DF82499D19E2A8A00D83BEC988DD5F57584A0ABBC",
      "statusBefore": "pending",
      "isSatisfiedBefore": false,
      "statusAfter": "pending",
      "isSatisfiedAfter": false
    },
    {
      "requirementId": "FR-PRF-003",
      "kind": "fr",
      "acId": "ac-02",
      "beforeText": "No cassette port: tape-related I/O port bits behave differently (cassette sense always reads \"no tape\").",
      "afterText": "The SX-64 board has no connected cassette port. Match pinned VICE's board-specific PLA inputs and suppress forwarding of motor, write and sense-out changes to tapeport devices. CPU-visible reads of bits 3-5 must still follow the native data, DDR and retained floating-capacitor state; neither permanently-high nor permanently-low input values are a valid universal substitute.",
      "alsoReplaceExactBodySentence": true,
      "expectedBodyOccurrences": 1,
      "bodyBeforeSha256": "AA8B6D7DD97A82B87E20BBE063A67A2A741DFF0CCD6DDBACD9B1AEC1E3FEFBE6",
      "statusBefore": "pending",
      "isSatisfiedBefore": false,
      "statusAfter": "pending",
      "isSatisfiedAfter": false
    },
    {
      "requirementId": "FR-PRF-003",
      "kind": "fr",
      "acId": "ac-04",
      "beforeText": "The 6510 I/O port bit 4 (cassette sense) is permanently pulled high.",
      "afterText": "For SX-64 CPU reads of $0001, each input-configured bit 3, 4 and 5 is replaced by its retained native data_set_bit value after native falloff processing. Reset clears those retained values. Output writes and output-to-input transitions seed the corresponding retained data bit, falloff flag and deadline as pinned VICE does. A flagged retained value clears on a read only when its stored deadline is strictly less than maincpu_clk: a charged input therefore remains charged at the exact deadline and clears on the first later read. Output-configured bits retain normal port readback. Match each bit independently, native RNG-dependent deadline selection, repeated writes, direction transitions, reset and read side effects; do not impose an always-high or always-zero sense bit.",
      "alsoReplaceExactBodySentence": true,
      "expectedBodyOccurrences": 1,
      "bodyBeforeSha256": "AA8B6D7DD97A82B87E20BBE063A67A2A741DFF0CCD6DDBACD9B1AEC1E3FEFBE6",
      "statusBefore": "pending",
      "isSatisfiedBefore": false,
      "statusAfter": "pending",
      "isSatisfiedAfter": false
    }
  ],
